For a graph $G$ on $n \ge 1$ vertices, the following are equivalent:

1. $G$ is a tree (connected with no cycles);
2. $G$ is connected and has $n - 1$ edges;
3. $G$ has no cycles and has $n - 1$ edges;
4. every two vertices of $G$ are joined by exactly one path.

In particular, tree on $n$ vertices $\iff$ connected with $n-1$ edges.
